==Strategy==
This stage is extremely barren and only consists of Mega-Mooth with a few peons once in a while, though they shouldn't be taken lightly if they do spawn, as they're generally tanky and boast high DPS.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]]: Fishman's fast foreswing, high speed and Massive Damage versus Floating allows it to easily cripple or even outright kill Mega-Mooth whenever if the peons aren't around, potentially enabling other units to rush the stage with terrifying ease.
*[[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]]: With the range and speed buffs from his True Form, Dumpling is able to hit Dagshund and create a Wave that chips down Mega-Mooth and the peons.
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]: Bahamut's extremely high damage can allow him to severely cripple either a peon or Mega-Mooth itself.
*[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]]: Can Double Bounty the Gabriel for a quick cash boost.
*[[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]]: Don't underestimate the Gory Dark here, as he hits 500% on the final stage. Pizza can deal serious damage to the Gory as well as hit Dagshund.

